# blacklist file for block-badips
#
# Each IPv4 or IPv6 address which is in a separate line will always be blocked
# by block-badips.sh, even if it is not on the downloaded list, unless it is in
# /etc/block-badips.whitelist. Ranges are not supported.
# Lines containing anything else, like these comments, are ignored.
#
# Examples:
#198.51.100.23
#2001:db8::23
